      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "si",
      "answerEn": "sí (‘yes’) or si (‘if’); Spanish Scrabble tiles omit the accent mark",
      "noteEn": "Standard Spanish distinguishes sí, ‘yes,’ from si, ‘if.’ Spanish Scrabble uses unaccented vowel tiles even for words that carry a written accent in ordinary text, so the played SI can represent either spelling. Without a sentence, the board alone does not choose between them.",
      "example": { "es": "Sí, iré si puedo.", "en": "Yes, I will go if I can." },
      "tags": ["word", "accent", "spelling", "board game", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-clitoris--printed-without-accent",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "clitoris",
      "answerEn": "clitoris; standard Spanish spells clítoris",
      "noteEn": "Spanish Scrabble uses unaccented vowel tiles even for words that carry a written accent in ordinary text, so the rack shows CLITORIS. Standard Spanish writes clítoris with an accent on the first í.",
      "example": { "es": "El clítoris forma parte de la anatomía genital.", "en": "The clitoris is part of genital anatomy." },
      "tags": ["word", "anatomy", "printed without accent", "spelling", "B1"]
    },
